      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lumberton began in 1894 as a stop on the Gulf, Beaumont and Kansas City Railway, sparking its early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumberton%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s post office opened in 1909, serving the local sawmills and lumber camps that defined its early economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumberton%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lumberton incorporated in July 1973, was briefly declared a non‑city after lawsuits in 1975, but later re‑incorporated with new boundaries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumberton%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city sits in southeastern Hardin County, its eastern edge following Village Creek, a tributary that feeds the Neches River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumberton%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Beaumont lies just 12 miles south of Lumberton, linking the town to the larger Beaumont–Port Arthur metropolitan area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
